/E (Sample efficiency in reinforcement learning refers to how many interactions an agent needs with its environment to learn a good, or optimal, policy. Algorithms with higher sample efficiency require fewer samples \(experiences\) to achieve a certain level of performance, which is crucial in real-world applications where data collection can be costly or time-consuming.)
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [1]
>>
