/K [0]
>>
endobj
745 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 400 0 R
/E (Deep Q-Networks \(DQN\) represent a significant breakthrough in reinforcement learning by successfully combining Q-Learning with deep neural networks. This integration allows agents to learn optimal policies in environments with high-dimensional state spaces, such as raw pixel data from video games, which was previously intractable for traditional Q-Learning.)
/Pg 28 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
746 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 400 0 R
/E (At its core, a DQN uses a neural network to approximate the Q-value function, Q\(s,a\). Instead of maintaining a large table of Q-values for each state-action pair, the network takes the state as input and outputs the Q-values for all possible actions in that state.)
/Pg 28 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
747 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /Figure
/P 400 0 R
/Pg 28 0 R
/A [2034 0 R 0]
/Alt (preencoded.png)
/K [3]
>>
endobj
