751 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 400 0 R
/T (Input State)
/E (Input State)
/Pg 28 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
752 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 400 0 R
/E (The network typically consists of several convolutional layers \(especially when dealing with image-based inputs\) followed by fully connected layers. The final output layer has one neuron for each possible action, with each neuron's activation representing the estimated Q-value for that action in the given state.)
/Pg 28 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
753 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 400 0 R
/E (The DQN is trained by minimizing a loss function, which measures the difference between the current Q-value prediction and a target Q-value. This target Q-value is derived from the Bellman equation, incorporating the immediate reward and the maximum Q-value of the next state:)
/Pg 28 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
