/P 407 0 R
/E (Policy Gradient \(PG\) methods represent a class of reinforcement learning algorithms that directly optimize the agent's policy, denoted as \\pi\(a|s; \\theta\), which is a function that maps states to a probability distribution over actions. This policy is parameterized by a set of weights \\theta. Instead of learning a value function to guide action selection, PG methods aim to find the optimal \\theta that maximizes the expected cumulative reward.)
/Pg 35 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
912 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 407 0 R
/E (The core idea is to adjust the policy parameters \\theta in the direction of the gradient of the expected reward. The policy gradient theorem provides a robust mathematical foundation for this, allowing for the computation of the gradient without explicitly differentiating through the environment's dynamics. The theorem states:)
/Pg 35 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
