/P 408 0 R
/E (A significant advantage of directly optimizing the policy is its natural applicability to environments with continuous action spaces. Unlike value-based methods that often require discretization of continuous actions, policy gradient methods can output continuous action probabilities or parameters for a continuous distribution \(e.g., mean and variance of a Gaussian distribution\), making them well-suited for tasks like robotic control or autonomous driving where precise, continuous movements are necessary.)
/Pg 36 0 R
/K [1]
>>
