/P 411 0 R
/E (Policy gradients are particularly well-suited for robotics due to their ability to handle continuous action spaces and generate smooth control signals. Unlike value-based methods that often require discretizing continuous actions, policy gradient methods can directly optimize policies that output continuous action values or parameters for continuous distributions \(e.g., mean and variance of a Gaussian distribution\). This is critical for robotic tasks that demand precise and fluid movements, where even small discontinuities can lead to instability or failure.)
/Pg 39 0 R
/K [9]
