1071 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 416 0 R
/E (A2C \(Advantage Actor-Critic\) is a synchronous, on-policy actor-critic method that combines policy gradient \(actor\) and value function approximation \(critic\) in a cohesive framework. It is essentially a synchronous version of A3C \(Asynchronous Advantage Actor-Critic\), where instead of multiple parallel agents collecting experiences asynchronously, a single agent or a set of agents collect experiences in a synchronous manner. This approach aims to reduce the variance of policy gradient estimates by using the critic's value function to estimate the advantage of actions.)
/Pg 44 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
