/E (A2C is often considered simpler to implement than A3C because it removes the complexities of asynchronous training across multiple threads or processes. It leverages the benefits of the actor-critic framework, such as lower variance updates compared to pure policy gradient methods, while maintaining a single, coherent training process. However, this simplicity comes at the cost of sample efficiency. Without the asynchronous exploration and decorrelation of experiences provided by multiple parallel agents in A3C, A2C may require more data or larger batch sizes to achieve comparable performance, especially in environments where exploration is challenging.)
