1115 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 417 0 R
/E (A3C \(Asynchronous Advantage Actor-Critic\) is an asynchronous, parallel actor-critic method that stands out for its efficiency and stability in various reinforcement learning tasks. Its key innovation lies in the use of multiple parallel agents, each interacting with its own copy of the environment, collecting experiences asynchronously, and updating a shared global network. This approach allows the algorithm to explore the environment more broadly and efficiently, leading to faster learning and improved performance.)
/Pg 45 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
1116 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 417 0 R
/E (The asynchronous updates are crucial for reducing correlation in the training data. Unlike synchronous methods where a single agent collects a batch of correlated experiences, A3C's parallel agents generate diverse and decorrelated trajectories. Each agent independently computes gradients based on its local experience and applies these gradients to the global network, preventing the updates from becoming stuck in local optima and improving the stability of the learning process.)
/Pg 45 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
