1260 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 421 0 R
/T (Key Takeaways: Evolution from Classical to Modern RL)
/E (Key Takeaways: Evolution from Classical to Modern RL)
/Pg 49 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
1261 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 421 0 R
/E (The field of Reinforcement Learning has evolved dramatically from classical methods, which relied heavily on explicit environment models and tabular representations, to modern deep RL approaches capable of tackling vast, continuous state and action spaces. This evolution has been driven by advancements in computational power and deep neural networks, enabling agents to learn complex behaviors directly from raw sensory input. The progression from Dynamic Programming to model-free methods, and then to integrating deep learning, highlights a continuous effort to overcome limitations in scalability, sample efficiency, and real-world applicability.)
/Pg 49 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
1262 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 421 0 R
/E (This journey underscores a transition from theoretical optimality in constrained environments to practical effectiveness in highly complex, uncertain domains. Each new paradigm builds upon its predecessors, addressing new challenges and expanding the reach of RL.)
/Pg 49 0 R
/K [3]
>>
